{"content":"h06.\n\n**Handlers** (RPC methods on `APIV1Service` that transitively trigger a webhook POST to a user-configured URL):\n\n- `APIV1Service.CreateMemo` — `server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go:70` → `DispatchMemoCreatedWebhook` → `dispatchMemoRelatedWebhook` (`server/router/api/v1/memo_service_webhooks.go:48`)\n- `APIV1Service.UpdateMemo` — `server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go:401` → `dispatchMemoUpdatedSideEffects` → `DispatchMemoUpdatedWebhook` → `dispatchMemoRelatedWebhook`\n- `APIV1Service.DeleteMemo` — `server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go:518` → `DispatchMemoDeletedWebhook` → `dispatchMemoRelatedWebhook`\n- `APIV1Service.CreateMemoComment` — `server/router/api/v1/memo_service_comments.go:20` → `DispatchMemoCommentCreatedWebhook` (`server/router/api/v1/memo_service_webhooks.go:30`)\n\n(also reachable indirectly: `SetMemoAttachments` and `SetMemoRelations`, both of which call `dispatchMemoUpdatedSideEffects`.)\n\nIn each case the URL is pulled from the user's stored webhook config (`s.Store.GetUserWebhooks(ctx, creatorID)`, `hook.Url`) and assigned into the outbound payload before dispatch.\n\n**Convergence function** — `webhook.Post` at `internal/webhook/webhook.go:120`\n\nAll dispatch paths call `webhook.PostAsync` (`internal/webhook/webhook.go:184`), which merely enqueues the payload onto `asyncPostQueue`; the fixed pool of worker goroutines started in `init()` (`internal/webhook/webhook.go:42-55`) pulls from that queue and calls `Post`, which is the single place that actually builds and issues the `http.Client.Do(req)` request (`safeClient.Do(req)`, line 152) to `requestPayload.URL` — the one point where every handler's path lands before an HTTP request is actually sent.","iteration":11,"turn":1,"type":"assistant"}
